      "text": "The average value, also known as the arithmetic mean, is calculated by summing all the values and dividing by the number of values. Let's denote the given numbers as \\(0\\), \\(2z\\), \\(4z\\), \\(8z\\), and \\(16z\\). The average value is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average} = \\frac{0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z}{5}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we sum the values:\n\n\\[\n0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z = (0 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16)z = 30z\n\\]\n\nNow, we divide the sum by the number of values, which is 5:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average} = \\frac{30z}{5} = 6z\n\\]\n\nThus, the average value is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6z}\n\\]",
